
-- What are functions in SQL?
-- Functions = Built in operations that perform a specific task inside a query 

-- Common Built in funcions 
-- ROUND(). Round a number to n decimals. 	Ex: SELECT ROUND(3.14159,2) --> 3.14
-- CEIL()/FLOOR(). Round up or down. 		Ex: SELECT CEIL(2.1): --> 3

-- Text Functions
-- UPPER(text). Converts text to uppercase 	Ex: SELECT UPPER(catagory)
-- LOWER(text). Converts to lowercase 		Ex: SELECT LOWER(product_name)
-- LENGTH(text). Returns character count 	Ex: SELECT LENGTH(product_name)

-- Date Function
-- NOW(). Returns our current timestamp		Ex: SELECT NOW();
-- CURRENT_DATE. Today's Date				Ex: SELECT CURRENT_DATE;
-- AGE(). Returns the diff between 2 dates	Ex: SELECT AGE('2026-10-20', '2000-05-15'); --> 25 yrs 5 mons 5 days

-- Date functions are often used for reports or logs



